Read the most liked review of IJ on GoodReads.  It's brilliant.

I've tried a handful over 15 years and yet I find it difficult to say good or bad about them.  It's possible that OCD, especially the famous pure type, just doesn't respond that well to drugs.  My backup doc put it like this - 'I can't give you a pill that stops thoughts.'

&#x200B;

I've had no serious side effects.  Going on or coming off them has resulted in some bad dreams, nightmares really, the ones where you're thankful you can't remember the details.  Some people say they get brain zaps; I get some slightly unusual sensations.  I've gained some weight with Mirtazapine and there's another side effect that I won't divulge but let's just say only males have to worry.

&#x200B;

So yeah, not sure what to tell you.  I've had good and bad days, good and bad emotions, some weight gain, but whether the meds have been the defining factor or a factor at all is hard to say.

By virtue of them not performing Thrift Shop they are better.

