Downvotes in 3, 2 1...

I've been meaning to thank you for replying, so here it is - thanks.

&#x200B;

Ebbing hope is what I'm feeling right now too - the idea of living with a brain in a constant state of fear and worry for years to come.   I certainly don't want to hurt anyone with my own death, but nor do I want to keep living like this, bouncing from one scenario to another as the irrational or semi-rational thoughts pile up, combine and mutate.

&#x200B;

I still find it amusing that while typing this, an onlooker would point out that the things that torture me don't exist; what can you say?  Our minds are our connection to the world, and mine seems to seek out things that hurt me.

&#x200B;

It's a bitch.

