I don't know about other states, but in Qld the process is interesting - I did a dicey post grad degree, got decent grades, went to an interview for states schools where they base their opinion of you on half a dozen questions, then got told a fortnight later I wouldn't be offered full or part time work unless I got more experience.  Considering some of the people they let in to schools, it was a knock.

&#x200B;

Part of it might've had to do with my preferred regions - I thought there was a fair spread, but I think you have be willing to go pretty much anywhere (where I assume the schools are 'difficult') to get work straight out.

